        "path": "home/home.ail.md",
        "text": "# Home page\n\nThe whole site is one page, read top to bottom. Its centre is the journey:\none sentence followed down every level of the real Tic-Tac-Toe spec.\n\n```ail\nnode HomePage : view   level: experience\n  why   One page that says what AIL is, shows it working on a real spec from the first sentence to the running game, and shows how to start.   <- AIL\n  what\n    the parts appear in this order: TopBar, Hero, GapStrip, TreeSection, Journey, WatchSection, Readers, BuildLoop, ReviewSection, AdoptSection, SpecBrowser, GetStarted, Footer\n    the top bar scrolls away with the page; nothing on the page is fixed or sticky\n    Scenario: one story, in order\n      Given the page is open\n      Then the level 1 heading reads \"Write one sentence. Watch it become working software.\"\n      And the level 2 headings read \"Between a prompt and the code, there is nothing to review.\", \"A tree of tasks, the same all the way down\", \"Follow one sentence all the way down\", \"Watch AIL build, and adopt\", \"One spec, four readers\", \"How a spec becomes code you can trust\", \"Review the spec and the screens. That's all.\", \"Already have an app? Adopt it.\", \"Browse the specs\" and \"Start in two minutes\", in that order\n    Scenario: every top bar link has a place to land\n      Given the page is open\n      Then the page has elements with the ids \"tree\", \"journey\", \"watch\", \"readers\", \"loop\", \"review\", \"adopt\", \"specs\" and \"start\"\n  look\n    page     a div: background color.page, color color.text, font.sans at font.body, line-height 1.6, min-height 100vh\n    layout   [ TopBar, main, Footer ]\n    main     a main element holding [ Hero, GapStrip, TreeSection, Journey, WatchSection, Readers, BuildLoop, ReviewSection, AdoptSection, SpecBrowser, GetStarted ], with no gaps between them; each section brings its own padding\n  uses      TopBar, Hero, GapStrip, TreeSection, Journey, WatchSection, Readers, BuildLoop, ReviewSection, AdoptSection, SpecBrowser, GetStarted, Footer\n  children  TopBar, Hero, GapStrip, TreeSection, Journey, WatchSection, Readers, BuildLoop, ReviewSection, AdoptSection, SpecBrowser, GetStarted, Footer\n```\n"
